    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d699">

                <pb facs="1175" n="1161" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 E. W./9–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-29T22:00:00+03:00">September 29,
                            1944—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 30—2:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3725. ReDepts 2232, September 18, 8 p.m. The British Ambassador having approached
                    the Soviet Government on the subject of the proposed declarations by Rumania,
                    Bulgaria and Hungary concerning the protection of refugees, I have informed
                    Molotov by letter <pb facs="1176" n="1162" xml:id="pg1162"/> that the United
                    States Government is in agreement with the purpose of the British proposal and
                    has no objection to the suggested text of the declaration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
